    <name>
      <text>Evaluate the Integral</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Evaluate the integral \[ \int {@p@} d{@v@}. \] [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:ans1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>
<p>For this question we will have to use the identity \[\displaystyle \sin(A)\cos(B) = \frac{1}{2} \left[ \sin(A+B) + \sin(A-B) \right] \] to simplify the expression as follows: </p>

<p> 
\[\begin{array}{rcl}\displaystyle {@p@} &\displaystyle = &\displaystyle {@rdm3@} \left( \frac{1}{2} \sin({@rdm1*v@} + {@rdm2*v@}) + \sin({@rdm1*v@} - {@rdm2*v@}) \right ) \\ 

&\displaystyle =&\displaystyle {@rdm3@}\left( {@q@}\right) \\ 
&\displaystyle =&\displaystyle {@rdm3*q@} \end{array}\] 
</p>
<p>
So, \[\begin{array}{rcl}\displaystyle \int {@p@} d{@v@} &\displaystyle =&\displaystyle \int {@rdm3*q@} d{@v@} \\ 
&\displaystyle =&\displaystyle {@int(rdm3*q,v)+c@} \end{array}\]</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
